  "decision_conditions": [
    "The roof form of the new dwelling, by virtue of its detailed design, siting, misalignment with the main dwelling and set down in roof ridge height, would appear visually intrusive, incongruous, and out of keeping with the character and appearance of the host property and the wider street scene. The proposal is therefore contrary to Section 12 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D4 and D5 of the London Plan (2021), Policy CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), and Policies DMD6,, DMD8, DMD13 and DMD37 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014).",
    "The proposed dropped kerb and parking arrangement for the new dwelling, by virtue of its location within 10m of a junction and its proximity to a telegraph pole, would result in harm to highway safety. The arrangement would adversely affect vehicle movements along Connaught Avenue and give rise to conditions prejudicial to the free flow and safety of vehicular traffic, as well as unsafe pedestrian movements. The proposal is therefore contrary to Section 9 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies T6 and T6.1 of the London Plan (2021), Policy CP25 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), Policy DMD46 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014) and the Revised Technical Standards for Footway Crossovers (2013)."
  ],
